    "q-347899": {
      "dom_id": "step-q347899",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2}+⋯$",
      "worked_solution": "The Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $3x$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & =(3x)-\\frac{(3x)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(3x)^{5}}{5!}-⋯ \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{27{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{243{x}^{5}}{120}-⋯ \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{81{x}^{5}}{40}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯ \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{24}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the expansions for $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(3x-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{81{x}^{5}}{40}-⋯)+(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{24}+⋯) \\\\  & =1+3x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
