    "q-350431": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350431",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-5x).$\n\n$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-5x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,\\frac{625{x}^{4}}{4}+⋯$",
      "worked_solution": "The Maclaurin series for $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-5x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-5x) & =(-5x)-\\frac{1}{2}(-5x)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(-5x)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(-5x)^{4}+⋯ \\\\  & =-5x-\\frac{25{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{125{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{625{x}^{4}}{4}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
