    "q-350458": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350458",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Find the first two non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-2x-8{x}^{2}).$\n\n$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-2x-8{x}^{2})=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,\\frac{56{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯$",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of logarithms, we observe that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-2x-8{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((1+2x)(1-4x)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+2x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x),$ we recall the standard result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x) & =x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo obtain the expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+2x),$ we replace $x$ with $2x$ in the standard expansion:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+2x) & =(2x)-\\frac{1}{2}(2x)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(2x)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(2x)^{4}+⋯ \\\\  & =2x-\\frac{1}{2}(4{x}^{2})+\\frac{1}{3}(8{x}^{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(16{x}^{4})+⋯ \\\\  & =2x-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}-4{x}^{4}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-4x),$ we replace $x$ with $-4x$ in the standard expansion:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-4x) & =(-4x)-\\frac{1}{2}(-4x)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(-4x)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(-4x)^{4}+⋯ \\\\  & =-4x-\\frac{1}{2}(16{x}^{2})+\\frac{1}{3}(-64{x}^{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(256{x}^{4})+⋯ \\\\  & =-4x-8{x}^{2}-\\frac{64{x}^{3}}{3}-64{x}^{4}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the two series to give the desired result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-2x-8{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+2x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-4x) \\\\  & =(2x-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}-⋯)+(-4x-8{x}^{2}-\\frac{64{x}^{3}}{3}-⋯) \\\\  & =(2-4)x+(-2-8){x}^{2}+(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{64}{3}){x}^{3}+⋯ \\\\  & =-2x-10{x}^{2}-\\frac{56{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
