    "q-350456": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350456",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Find the first two non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+3x}{1-3x}).$\n\n$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+3x}{1-3x})=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,\\frac{486{x}^{5}}{5}+⋯$",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of logarithms, we observe that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+3x}{1-3x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3x)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x),$ we recall the standard result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x) & =x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo obtain the expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3x),$ we replace $x$ with $3x$ in the standard expansion:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3x) & =(3x)-\\frac{1}{2}(3x)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(3x)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(3x)^{4}+\\frac{1}{5}(3x)^{5}-⋯ \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{1}{2}(9{x}^{2})+\\frac{1}{3}(27{x}^{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(81{x}^{4})+\\frac{1}{5}(243{x}^{5})-⋯ \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{2}+9{x}^{3}-\\frac{81{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{243{x}^{5}}{5}-⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-3x),$ we replace $x$ with $-3x$ in the standard expansion:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-3x) & =(-3x)-\\frac{1}{2}(-3x)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(-3x)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(-3x)^{4}+\\frac{1}{5}(-3x)^{5}-⋯ \\\\  & =-3x-\\frac{1}{2}(9{x}^{2})+\\frac{1}{3}(-27{x}^{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(81{x}^{4})+\\frac{1}{5}(-243{x}^{5})-⋯ \\\\  & =-3x-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{2}-9{x}^{3}-\\frac{81{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{243{x}^{5}}{5}-⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we subtract the two series to give the desired result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+3x}{1-3x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3x)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-3x) \\\\  & =(3x-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{2}+9{x}^{3}-\\frac{81{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{243{x}^{5}}{5}\\,-) \\\\  & -(-3x-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{2}-9{x}^{3}-\\frac{81{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{243{x}^{5}}{5}-⋯) \\\\  & =(3+3)x+(-\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{9}{2}){x}^{2}+(9+9){x}^{3} \\\\  & +(-\\frac{81}{4}+\\frac{81}{4}){x}^{4}+(\\frac{243}{5}+\\frac{243}{5}){x}^{5}+⋯ \\\\  & =6x+18{x}^{3}+\\frac{486{x}^{5}}{5}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
